vash news (release notes)

2.1.4
  * linlib: cursor moving on r_page(): simple wrap columns and rows
  * linlib: more clear navigation on r_page()

2.1.3
  * .vash_history is default vash history cache file
  * mode to save or sync history cache in home directory
  * hide from on-line setup flag for mail checking
  
2.1.2
  * source and rc files cleaning

2.1.1.dev
  * new design of invocation parameters
  * job control
  * resizing hwframe
  * preprocessing rc-files (predef=1 if BSD-like system)
  * support of repeat a last command with single key macro
  * fix optimization of main menu rebuilding
  * memory for main menu: auto allocation

2.0.33
  * total rewrite source confirming ANSI syntax
  * config preprocessor implemented

2.0.32
  * revise rc files
  * FreeBSD 13.3 compiling 

2.0.31
  * repair calculation of UTF-8 visible length in main menu rendering

2.0.30
  * rchelp() draft, yet incomplete
  * PgUp+PgDown support for main menu
  * KH+KE in main menu
  * add script MK-binlocal.sh

2.0.29
2.0.28
  * no extra w_line on u_menu
  * mark & select dialogues cleanup
  * fix e2k
  * fix regression of FreeBSD port
  * strverscmp() from GNU come back

2.0.27 -- 18 Apr 2004
  * FreeBSD support revailed, checked on 1.2-RELEASE
  * vhset manual added
  * add flag to disable #@ marker show
  * actualize copyright notes and files
  
2.0.26 -- 3 Apr 2024
  * support for '#@' substution both in rc files and in command editor
  * rc files macro for cursor positioning in editor template
  * /etc/vhset/xterm-256color now installed as symlink
  * fix of typo and inaccuracy in help files

2.0.25 -- 22 Mar 2024
  * support for legacy 8bit encodings is completed
  * repair recognition of non-ascii symbols in rc files
  * added setup flag: anyway sh -c
  * some bugfix and help pages cleanup
  * actualize docs: COMPILE, README, PLAN, WISHES

2.0.24b -- Feb 2024
  * first release on sourceforge.net with binary packages for x86_64(amd64)
